(Note 1: I played Hack as early as 1989, but was dreadful at it. 
Started on NetHack in 1996, ascended a few times with savescumming in
my first six months of playing, stopped savescumming, finally truly
ascended in 2000, three times within a month, haven't ascended since. 
Until now.)

(Note 2: This is from memory, except the ending stats which were
written down, as I am superstitious and believe any character I take
more than basic notes on is doomed to failure.)

Lesson of the day: Sometimes, the RNG just plain giveth.

Leyla the Elven Priestess started out acceptable, with a 14 Int and
spellbooks of Protection and Extra Healing.  Can't remember anything
remarkable about the early-game, except that I found a (BoH and "AoR
before Sokoban.  Also got lucky on spellbooks, getting Identify,
Remove Curse, Polymorph, Fireball, Charm Monster, Magic Mapping, and a
couple more quite early.  Unfortunately, due to an overflowing
fountain in Minetown, she accidentally walked right into a pool of
water and blanked most of them before they were read (damn
mouse-click-walking!)

Due to a rusty mace and having a Magic Lamp, I went ahead and wished
her up Mjollnir, hoping on another spellbook of Light (which I didn't
see until Gehennom, natch).  Things started to look pretty bright.

Then the sun just plain exploded.  I had lost a completely ascendable
Wizard to some really bad luck with a pissed-off God and a wide-angle
death ray (or is it disintegration?) on around DLVL 15.  Miraculously,
not only did that character leave bones, but I found them in this
game.  I almost felt bad about looting Magicbane, an entire full AK
including SDSM, [CoMR, [GoD, [HoB, speed boots, and a still-blessed
BoH containing ~30 Holy Waters, ~60 blank scrolls, and ~20 good gems. 
If I could have, I would have grabbed the Eye, but I'm guessing I
couldn't pick it up because the Wizard had been N and I was C.

Then I remembered how I had felt when I had lost said Wizard, stopped
feeling bad, and thumbed my nose in the RNG's general direction.

Needless to say, the game became ridiculously easy at that point.  The
bones also had yielded =oSD, =oL and three magic markers, so I didn't
even have anything to wish for.  By the Castle, I had been crowned,
granted both Fire and Frost Brand, and even found Sunsword in the
castle weapon-room.  I believe this was my luckiest game ever in terms
of sheer loot.

It wasn't perfect, however.  I had a =oTC but ran into suspiciously
few leprechauns or nymphs, and in the entire game only encountered
three Tengu, so I didn't get jumpy until near the endgame.

The Quest, of course, was both tedious and easy.  Better than
frustrating and difficult, though, so onward.

I experienced a panic in the Castle while using the A command to
continue disrobing.  Since I don't even do save-backups anymore (lazy,
but I've only ever Panicked a few times and never lost a character to
a general Windows crash) I was almost devestated - until I noticed
that the files were intact, allowing a Restore.  OK, I did the Castle
once, I can do it again, especially since I'd found a ring of
Conflict.

The best wishes I could think of were just for some more magic markers
and a blessed spellbook of magic mapping which, if I had bothered to
remember I had already ID'd, I could have just written anyway.  I
could have gone for the Master Key of Thievery, but really, I just
couldn't bring myself to be THAT abusive.

Disaster struck when fighting Rodney - after I killed him once over
land, and noticed he dropped the Book, I thought "Well, it's alright
to kill this copy he summoned over water".  About ten turns later, and
I notice the Mitre of Holiness is gone.  D'oh.  I always forget that
he steals quest artifacts.  I had left an "AoMB in the Castle (that is
the only way to retrieve items from underwater, correct?) so I weighed
my options.  I could backtrack an insane amount to get the Mitre back,
or I could just use my last wish on a plain HoB.  I chose the latter
path.

Only afterwards did it occur to me that I could simply have wished for
an "AoMB.  Really, NetHack doth make fools of us all sometimes.

By the endgame I had reached level 21 - quite modest for a Priest.  No
luck with Wraiths and only a few !oGL in the whole game.

The way out of the dungeon was almost eerily quiet.  Rodney only
appeared twice, getting a shot from Orcus' /WoD both times.  Magicbane
ate most of my curses.

Decent potion luck had gotten my HP up to ~246, and boy did I need it,
even though I didn't think I would.  More on that later.

Earth was simple - zap Rodney, dig, blink, gone.

Took me awhile to find the portal on Air (no crystal balls and I never
was good at the scroll tricks) so I had to take out a few Air
Elementals.  No big deal.  Got down to maybe 80 HP once, but came out
of it swinging.

Fire - a breeze.  There was one Archon, but I just sidestepped with a
blindfold on once I had seen a monster disappear into the portal.

Water - not as bad as usual.  Portal was found pretty quick and easy.

OK, so the astral plane - oy.  On entry, I genocided S and a, so I
could just sidestep around many of the Priests and Angels.  Went for
Famine's side first - no dice.

Tried the middle, with Death, next.  I really do not remember Death
being such a pain.  He took my max HP all the way down to 168. 
Somehow, I had forgotten that he even does that at all.  In heated
battle with him and Angels, my one and only "oLS got used up.  I had,
in utter and complete stupidity, forgotten to save a few !oFH and my
spell points ran out very fast casting Extra Healing with the "oY.

Thank God (literally), the middle altar WAS the correct one, and with
an almost reverential feeling, I hit alt-O.

Final stats (I'm no good at screenshotting):

St: 18  Dx: 22  Co: 16  In: 21  Wi: 22  Ch: 14
Max HP: 168    Max MP: 288  AC: -44  Lv: 21  Turn: 38,859

Notable kills:
Aasmodeus, Baalzebub, Orcus, Yeenoghu, Juiblex, Rodney (6 times, 3 of
which were the initial battle with him), Death (thrice), Famine
(twice).

Genocided: a S g h L R.  I usually don't bother with h, but a "faint
wave of psychic energy" near the endgame made me paranoid, and I had
more than enough scrolls and markers anyhow.  Ditto with R - I just
hate disenchanters.

In Bag at endgame were Ogresmasher, Trollsbane, Sunsword,
Stormbringer, Orcrist, Fire Brand, Frost Brand, and a lot of gems.

Final point total: 3,886,220

Whew.

